course: dictionary
lesson: 11096
title: Wheelbarrow: a cart and a lever
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A wheelbarrow is a small cart with one wheel at the front, two handles and two legs at the back. People use it to carry loads such as soil, sand or bricks. The words around a word give clues: «push a wheelbarrow» tells you it is something you push, and «a barrowful» tells you it holds a load.
explain: Look at how a sentence about the wheel works. «In a wheelbarrow the wheel is the pivot, and the load is easiest to lift when it sits close to the wheel.» A pivot is the point a lever turns around, so the clue is that the wheel is where the cart balances. Swap in your meaning to check it fits.
explain: Science gives the word a second meaning. «A see-saw, scissors, a bottle opener and a wheelbarrow all use levers.» A wheelbarrow is a lever: when you lift the handles, a heavy load feels lighter. Ask yourself: does the new meaning still make sense in the sentence? If it does, you have found the right one.
fact: A wheelbarrow is a small cart with one wheel, two handles and two legs.
fact: Wheelbarrows carry soil, sand or bricks in gardens and on building sites.
fact: In science, a wheelbarrow is a lever: the wheel is the pivot, and the load sits in the middle.
fact: In PE, a «wheelbarrow race» is when one child walks on their hands while a partner holds their legs.
fact: «Seesaws, scissors, wheelbarrows, bottle openers, nutcrackers, tongs and even your own arm are all levers.»
exercise: «A see-saw, scissors, a bottle opener and a wheelbarrow all use levers.» What is a lever? | A long, thin rope | A kind of garden hose | A sort of brick | *A simple machine that turns on a pivot to make lifting easier
exercise: In «the wheel is the pivot», what does pivot mean? | The handle you hold | *The point a lever turns around | The load you carry | The two legs at the back
exercise: Which of these is a wheelbarrow? | A bicycle with three wheels | *A small cart with one wheel and two handles | A tall ladder for painting | A tray for serving tea
test: In a «wheelbarrow race», what does one child do? | Rides a bike around the field | Sits on the grass | *Walks on their hands while a partner holds their legs | Carries a bucket of water
test: Why does a wheelbarrow make a heavy load feel lighter? | The wheel is made of metal | The load is kept in the legs | *Lifting the handles works as a lever | It has no wheel at all
exam: «A barrowful will do, to begin with» means | A very tall barrel | An empty box | *A wheelbarrow full | A small bird
